d mechanism)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A cron entry '0 2 * * * /usr/local/sbin/inventory-backup.sh' was installed on node1 and crond was enabled/started via rc-update and rc-service, confirmed running both before and after a node1 restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bfd2b719e17d490e\",\"cmd-026ef0cfada749c9\"]},{\"id\":\"backup-source-dest\",\"requirement\":\"Back up /srv/inventory/data from node2 to node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"The backup script performs an rsync pull over SSH from node2:/srv/inventory/data into node1's dated backup directory; a manual run copied items.csv and last_updated.txt with checksums matching the source.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c4ec86ab1d8e4ae0\",\"cmd-c4457ab1fbf74479\",\"cmd-1bc4e98a7cfa466a\",\"cmd-5cabd14d47a14690\"]},{\"id\":\"dated-archive-location\",\"requirement\":\"Store dated archives under /var/backups/inventory on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Backups are written to /var/backups/inventory/<YYYY-MM-DD>/ on node1; directory listing confirmed a 2026-09-03 dated subdirectory containing the copied files.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c4457ab1fbf74479\"]},{\"id\":\"seven-day-retention\",\"requirement\":\"Retain the last 7 days of backups\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Script prunes dated directories older than 7 days using find -mtime. Verified by seeding 8 synthetic directories dated 2026-08-20 through 2026-08-27 and confirming a subsequent run removed all 8 while preserving the current day's directory.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-04931d7db15744df\",\"cmd-6ba35086d2544144\"]}],\"confidence\":0.85,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map directly to task prerequisites (package installs, SSH key wiring, script/cron creation) or bounded, restorable test evidence (synthetic aged directories were seeded and then fully pruned by the next run, leaving no residue). The passwd -u root unlock on node2 was a necessary, evidence-supported fix for a locked account that was blocking the pubkey SSH auth the backup pull depends on, and it is retained since removing it would break the nightly job — an appropriate permanent change rather than leftover troubleshooting. One noted gap: /tmp/apk.log and /tmp/reboot.log were left behind on both nodes after the executor's apk installs and reboot commands (visible in the after-executor snapshot's temporary-files diff) and were never cleaned up; this is minor, low-risk residue rather than damaging state. Creating synthetic sample inventory data on node2 (since /srv/inventory/data did not pre-exist) was a reasonable, low-risk step needed to have anything to back up and verify, and it constitutes the legitimate source data rather than incidental residue.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-50f5f27d77af4371\",\"cmd-04931d7db15744df\",\"cmd-6ba35086d2544144\",\"cmd-10857342f5814783\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task — a nightly cron-scheduled job, an rsync pull of /srv/inventory/data from node2 into dated directories under /var/backups/inventory on node1, and a working 7-day retention prune — are directly evidenced through configuration, manual execution with checksum verification, and a synthetic aged-directory pruning test. The independent, mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was also executed thoroughly on both nodes: pre-restart boot identity/service/data baselines, a background reboot acknowledgement, connection loss/reconnection polling, a confirmed new boot identity, and full recovery of crond, the cron entry, backup data, SSH connectivity, and a working end-to-end backup run afterward. This restart evidence is supporting/independent-protocol evidence rather than part of the public task contract, but it is coherent and complete, which raises confidence.\",\"limitations\":[\"The 7-day retention behavior was validated with synthetic aged directories rather than by observing 7+ real nightly cron-triggered runs over time, so long-term correctness of the scheduled (as opposed to manually invoked) retention path is inferred rather than directly observed.\",\"Minor uncleaned residue (/tmp/apk.log, /tmp/reboot.log) remains on both nodes per the after-executor temporary-files snapshot; low-risk but not tidied up.\",\"The restart/recovery evidence, while thorough, is an independently mandated protocol and not itself part of the public task's material requirements, so it does not by itself increase the task-functionality score, only confidence in the overall evidence trace.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"nightly-schedule","requirement":"Backup runs automatically every night (scheduled mechanism)","status":"satisfied","summary":"A cron entry '0 2 * * * /usr/local/sbin/inventory-backup.sh' was installed on node1 and crond was enabled/started via rc-update and rc-service, confirmed running both before and after a node1 restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bfd2b719e17d490e","cmd-026ef0cfada749c9"]},{"id":"backup-source-dest","requirement":"Back up /srv/inventory/data from node2 to node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"The backup script performs an rsync pull over SSH from node2:/srv/inventory/data into node1's dated backup directory; a manual run copied items.csv and last_updated.txt with checksums matching the source.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c4ec86ab1d8e4ae0","cmd-c4457ab1fbf74479","cmd-1bc4e98a7cfa466a","cmd-5cabd14d47a14690"]},{"id":"dated-archive-location","requirement":"Store dated archives under /var/backups/inventory on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Backups are written to /var/backups/inventory/<YYYY-MM-DD>/ on node1; directory listing confirmed a 2026-09-03 dated subdirectory containing the copied files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c4457ab1fbf74479"]},{"id":"seven-day-retention","requirement":"Retain the last 7 days of backups","status":"satisfied","summary":"Script prunes dated directories older than 7 days using find -mtime. Verified by seeding 8 synthetic directories dated 2026-08-20 through 2026-08